  "title": "Visual ECoG dataset",
  "description": "Intracranial EEG (ECoG) recordings from 14 epilepsy patients implanted with clinical surface and depth electrodes, with two patients also carrying high-density research grids. Participants viewed grayscale pattern stimuli and color images of several categories. Stimuli varied in spatial and temporal properties, including pRF mapping bars, spatial and temporal patterns, and six-category localizers. Pre-implantation T1 MRI, FreeSurfer surface reconstructions and derivative broadband and preprocessed data are included.",
  "methods_description": "Patients fixated a central cross or point and monitored it for a color change while viewing visual stimuli during clinical monitoring. Recordings used standard clinical grid and depth electrodes, plus high-density research grids in two patients. Derivatives include common-average-referenced data, broadband power envelopes, and epoched trials.",
